{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The board could ask:\n\n- **Selection:** How was the exchange and lead market maker (LMM) selected? What alternatives were considered, and were commercial terms, conflicts, and the basis for the recommendation documented? What measurable quoting, spread, depth, and uptime commitments apply—and what happens if they are missed?\n- **Relevant-market expertise:** What experience does the LMM have in this ETF’s asset class, strategy, underlying-market hours and liquidity, and creation/redemption process? How will it manage volatile or stressed markets, and what staffing, systems, inventory, and escalation arrangements will it provide?\n- **Capital and seed support:** What initial capital or seed inventory is the LMM expected to provide, on what terms, for how long, and with what limits or obligations? Is support committed or discretionary, and what happens if it is withdrawn? Separately, what evidence supports expectations for durable investor demand and assets?\n\nTreat any seed from a market maker as potentially temporary trading or inventory support—not as evidence of lasting investor assets. These are suggested diligence questions for the board’s consideration, not a mandatory checklist or approval rule."}}
